  "details": "As things work currently, if you globally hide an avatar, it only stays hidden if you are using the shield mode in avatar display. \n\nI have all my friends manually shown because I have settings regarding avatar performance and file size specified that my friends go over, and sometimes distance-based hiding. This works great for me because I hide poor avatars and anyone far from me in large instances, and because my friends are always shown, I can see them from a distance or know their avatars well enough to feel safe having their poor avatars shown. The problem is, I just do not like certain avatars, and I do not want to see them regardless of who is wearing them, but I do not want to be rude and tell someone to stop using an avatar just because I don't personally like it. If one of my friends switches into one of those avatars, I have to manually hide them specifically and then check to see if they have changed out of it by showing them again. I would really appreciate having globally hidden avatars take priority over manually showing users so this isn't an issue.",
